  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up a socialised model of domestic waste and plastics management - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DWP5C Phase 2 builds on, deepens, and scales up the intervention&#x2019;s achievements, lessons and good practices obtained over the course of the implementation of Phase 1. It also utilises the results of the UNDP RIM-2020 survey, the rapid impact assessment conducted with Women&#x2019;s Unions, and the informal sector research conducted in Da Nang.
The project&#x2019;s outcome 1 is &#x201C;sustainable pilot models of waste management that improve livelihoods of waste workers (with a focus on women informal workers (IWW))&#x201D;. The Output 1.1 is &#x201C;Series of Interventions to empower IWW, and strengthen their resilience to withstand shocks, including the impacts of COVID-19 implemented&#x201D;.</narrative>
  </description>
